# ── piw environment configuration ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy this file to .local/env, fill in your keys, and piw reads it.
#
#   cp .env.example .local/env
#   $EDITOR .local/env
#   piw ~/my-project
#
# NOTE: .local/ is gitignored. Keep your keys out of version control.
#
# ── API Keys ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment and set the providers you use. pi resolves $VAR references in
# models.json at runtime, so these flow through automatically.

# SILICONFLOW_API_KEY=sk-...
# FIREWORKS_API_KEY=fw_...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-...
# HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY=hf_...

# ── Manifest locations ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# piw reads two files under .local/. piw seeds both on first run and
# never overwrites them.
#
#   .local/mise/config.toml   the [tools] manifest, parsed by mise
#   .local/piw.conf           the layer manifest, parsed by piw
#
# The env file holds secrets only. Host-side settings move to the shell
# environment or to the manifests.
